Journey: The virtualized My claims grid shows exactly the database's rows
Id: claims-grid-matches-db
Tags: @portal @grid @integration @regression
Role: commercial
Risk: 4
Requirements: PORTAL-7, PORTAL-8
Description: 420 claims in a virtualized ARIA grid (only ~18 rows exist in the DOM at a time). Every row, every column is compared with the database; then filter, sort and row navigation.

Run query "CUSTOMER_CLAIMS_AS_SHOWN" on claims with customer_id="C-1003" as dbRows
Count the rows of query "SELECT id FROM claims WHERE customer_id = 'C-1003'" on claims as total
Count the rows of query "SELECT id FROM claims WHERE customer_id = 'C-1003' AND status = 'REJECTED'" on claims as rejected

Log in
Click the "My claims" link
  Expect the page contains "${total} claims"
Capture all rows of the My claims grid as uiRows
Expect rows uiRows equal rows dbRows by key "Claim"

# The grid's own filtering and sorting agree with the data
Expect the My claims grid to have ${rejected} rows where Status is "Rejected"
Select "Rejected" from the "Status filter" dropdown
  Expect the page contains "${rejected} claims"
Sort the My claims grid by Amount descending
Expect the Amount column of the My claims grid to be sorted descending
Get the first row of query "SELECT id, printf('%.2f', amount_claimed) AS amount FROM claims WHERE customer_id = 'C-1003' AND status = 'REJECTED' ORDER BY amount_claimed DESC LIMIT 1" on claims as biggest
Expect the Amount of the row where Claim is "${biggest.id}" in the My claims grid to be "${biggest.amount}"

# Open a claim from deep inside the virtualized list
Select "All statuses" from the "Status filter" dropdown
Scroll the My claims grid to the row where Claim is "CLM-100003"
In the My claims grid, click "CLM-100003" in the row where Claim is "CLM-100003"
  Expect the URL contains "/app/claims/CLM-100003"
Expect testid=claim-policy has text "POL-H-109000"
